  "question": {
    "text": "The roots of the quadratic equation $x^2-2 \\sqrt{3} x-22=0$ are :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "imaginry",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "real, rational and equal",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "real, irrational and unequal",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "real, rational and unequal",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\text { Hints: } \\begin{aligned}\n& x^2-2 \\sqrt{3}-22=0 \\\\\n& D=12+(4 \\times 22)>0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$\\because$ coeffs are irrational,\n$$\nx=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{3} \\pm \\sqrt{12+88}}{2}\n$$\n$\\therefore$ Roots are irrational, real, unequal."
  }
